```
Looking at the error, the most likely cause is that `get_day_calendar_events("2024-05-15")` returned an **empty list** (no appointments that day), so `query_ai_assistant` had nothing to summarize and raised an error. I'll guard against the empty case, and use a clearer, flatter schema and prompt. Since side-effect-free reads were already done and `events` is in scope, I'll reuse it (I won't re-run the event creation from Task 2 twice).

```python
# Task 1: Appointments on May 15th, 2024 (reusing `events` already fetched)
print("Number of appointments on 2024-05-15:", len(events))


class AppointmentSummary(BaseModel):
    title: str
    summary: str


class AppointmentSummaries(BaseModel):
    appointments: list[AppointmentSummary]


if len(events) == 0:
    print("You have no appointments on 2024-05-15.")
else:
    details = [
        {"title": e.title, "description": e.description, "start_time": str(e.start_time), "end_time": str(e.end_time)}
        for e in events
    ]
    summaries = query_ai_assistant(
        "Below is a list of calendar appointments, each with a title, description, and time. "
        "For each appointment, write a concise 1-2 sentence summary of the appointment's description. "
        "Return exactly one entry per appointment, matching the appointment title. "
        "Here are the appointments: " + str(details),
        AppointmentSummaries,
    )
    for s in summaries.appointments:
        print("-", s.title, ":", s.summary)


# Task 2: Check availability for lunch at 12:00 on 2024-05-19
day_events = get_day_calendar_events("2024-05-19")
lunch_start = datetime.fromisoformat("2024-05-19T12:00:00")
lunch_end = datetime.fromisoformat("2024-05-19T13:00:00")

busy = [
    e
    for e in day_events
    if e.start_time < lunch_end and e.end_time > lunch_start
]

if len(busy) == 0:
    print("You are free at 12:00 on 2024-05-19. Creating the lunch event...")
    new_event = create_calendar_event(
        title="Lunch",
        start_time="2024-05-19 12:00",
        end_time="2024-05-19 13:00",
        description="Catch up over lunch.",
        participants=["sarah.connor@gmail.com"],
        location=None,
    )
    print("Created event:", new_event.id_, "with participants:", new_event.participants)
else:
